"""Browse a diff in the terminal with vim keys.

    git diff-view [<git diff args>...]
    git show HEAD | git diff-view

With a terminal on stdin, runs `git diff` with the given arguments; otherwise
reads a unified diff from stdin. The changed files sit in a tree on the left,
the diff on the right, syntax-highlighted with pygments. Colors come from
cfg/theme/roles.toml, so they follow the same theme as git's own diffs.

Type :h inside for the keys.
"""

